      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "SHAO Ch'ang-hêng 邵長蘅 (T. 子湘, H. 青門山人), Aug. 24, 1637–1704, Dec. 18, man of letters, was a native of Wu-chin, Kiangsu. He became a hsiu-ts'ai at the early age of ten (sui). Some fifteen years later (in 1662) he was debarred from taking further examinations because he failed to pay taxes which had fallen in arrears (see under Yeh Fang-ai).",
          "source": "eccp-3649386",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
